  "cleaning_decision": {
    "basis": "data_profile",
    "rationale": "Known variable roles and pre16 raw profile guide distinct methods: capacity is a stable continuous measurement with approximately symmetric within-entity variation, so use mean; spend is a nonnegative heavy-tailed measurement, so use median for a robust baseline; correlated_metric has meaningful numeric similarity features with fit-only within-entity Pearson r(signal_x)=0.825025, r(signal_z)=-0.558171, so use KNN on these two features, with same-entity donors/scales. Region is nominal onehot, plan has prespecified bronze/silver/gold order, channel labels are category identifiers; comments are presegmented lexical text using fit-only TFIDF. Activity and numeric predictors remain unfilled in the primary analysis. No truth or heldout values choose these methods. Prespecified sensitivity only: additionally mean-fill activity from pre16 same-entity data, retaining imputation markers and excluding filled windows."
  },
